title: Universities strike!
subtitle: Students demand a 30% reduction in tuition fees.
new-page: true
tags: event
role: event
face-image: img/events/vaga_students.jpeg
max-visits: 1
view-if: strike_triggered = "university" and not cat_caretaker_gov and education_spending >= -2 and education_spending < 3
on-arrival: {!
    Q.strike_timer = 6;
    Q.strike_university_response = null;
    Q.strike_university_settled = false;
    Q.strike_university_partner = Q.education_minister_party;
    if (["indp.", "ind.", "independent"].includes(Q.strike_university_partner)) Q.strike_university_partner = Q.president_party;
    if (Q.strike_university_partner == "ciu") Q.strike_university_partner = Q.parlament_current_ciu;
    if (Q.strike_university_partner == "federal_left") Q.strike_university_partner = Q.parlament_current_icv;
    Q.strike_university_relations = Q[Q.strike_university_partner + "_relations"];
    if (["jxsi", "jxcat"].includes(Q.strike_university_partner) && !Number.isFinite(Q.strike_university_relations))
        Q.strike_university_relations = Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_relations"];
!}

= Universities strike!

University students are on strike across Catalonia, demanding a 30% tuition fee reduction, with public funding replacing lost revenue for universities. Catalan university fees are the highest in Spain, a difference that is specially notable when looking at Masters' degrees. With streets flooded and university and research centres paralyzed, pressure is mounting against [? if education_minister_gender = "m": Conseller ?][? if education_minister_gender = "f": Consellera ?]of Education [+ education_minister +]. What will our position be?

- @accept
- @pressure
- @protest
- @quiet

@accept
title: Accept the students' demands
view-if: education_minister_party = player_party or (player_in_jxsi and education_minister_party = "jxsi") or (player_in_jxcat and education_minister_party = "jxcat")
subtitle: We control the ministry after all. \[-1 budget\]
choose-if: government_budget >= 1 and education_spending >= 0 and social_spending_cap >= 0 and not fla_escalated
unavailable-subtitle: [? if government_budget < 1: Not enough budget. ?][? if education_spending < 0: Education cuts need to be reversed before such a measure would even be possible. ?][? if social_spending_cap < 0: The current social spending cap is too low to allow for this. ?][? if fla_escalated: Stringent FLA conditions ban us from taking such action. ?]
on-arrival: strike_university_response = "accept"
go-to: resolve

@pressure
title: Push [+ education_minister_party +] to accept the students' demands
view-if: not (education_minister_party = player_party or (player_in_jxsi and education_minister_party = "jxsi") or (player_in_jxcat and education_minister_party = "jxcat")) and ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting)))
subtitle: We'll have to apply pressure on [+ education_minister_party +] for them to even consider sitting down with the union representatives. \[-1 resources; -1 budget\].
choose-if: (not (education_minister_party = player_party or (player_in_jxsi and education_minister_party = "jxsi") or (player_in_jxcat and education_minister_party = "jxcat")) and ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting)))) and party_resources >= 1 and ((difficulty < 0 and strike_university_relations >= 45) or (difficulty >= 0 and strike_university_relations >= 55)) and government_budget >= 1 and education_spending >= 0 and social_spending_cap >= 0 and not fla_escalated
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting))): We are not part of the government nor providing external support to it. ?][? if party_resources < 1: Not enough resources. ?][? if ((difficulty < 0 and strike_university_relations < 45) or (difficulty >= 0 and strike_university_relations < 55)): Our relations with [+ strike_university_partner +] are not good enough. ?][? if government_budget < 1: Not enough budget. ?][? if education_spending < 0: Education cuts need to be reversed before such a measure would even be possible. ?][? if social_spending_cap < 0: The current social spending cap is too low to allow such a measure. ?][? if fla_escalated: Stringent FLA conditions ban us from taking such action. ?]
on-arrival: strike_university_response = "pressure"
go-to: resolve

@protest
title: Join the protests!
choose-if: not ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting)))
unavailable-subtitle: We're not welcome here, as we are currently supporting the government they are protesting against.
on-arrival: strike_university_response = "protest"
go-to: resolve

@quiet
title: [? if (player_party = "erc" and erc_in_gob) or (player_party = "cup" and cup_in_gob) or (player_in_jxsi and jxsi_in_gob) or (player_in_jxcat and jxcat_in_gob): Back our partner's handling of the strike?][? if not ((player_party = "erc" and erc_in_gob) or (player_party = "cup" and cup_in_gob) or (player_in_jxsi and jxsi_in_gob) or (player_in_jxcat and jxcat_in_gob)) and ((player_party = "erc" and erc_supporting) or (player_party = "cup" and cup_supporting) or (player_in_jxsi and jxsi_supporting) or (player_in_jxcat and jxcat_supporting)): Leave this to the Generalitat to deal with?][? if not ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting))): Stay on the sidelines?]
on-arrival: strike_university_response = "quiet"
go-to: resolve

@resolve
on-arrival: {!
    var response = Q.strike_university_response;
    var option = this.game.scenes['strike_university.' + response];
    var delivery = response == "accept" || response == "pressure";
    if (Q.strike_triggered == "university" && !Q.cat_caretaker_gov &&
        Q.education_spending >= -2 && Q.education_spending < 3 &&
        option && this._runPredicate(option.viewIf, true) && this._runPredicate(option.chooseIf, true)) {
        var controlled = [Q.player_party].concat(Q.player_in_jxsi ? ["jxsi"] : [], Q.player_in_jxcat ? ["jxcat"] : []);
        Q.strike_triggered = null;
        Q.strike_university_settled = delivery;
        if (delivery) {
            Q.government_budget -= 1;
            if (response == "pressure") Q.party_resources -= 1;
            G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"university_tuition_agreement", title:"University should not be a privilege",
                fiscal_ticks:12,
                description:"Public funding replaces a 30% reduction in university tuition fees.",
                targets:{welfare_index_growth:0.05, social_dissent_eq:-1, generalitat_surplus:-0.01}});
            if ((Q.cat_coalition || []).concat(Q.cat_coalition_support || []).some(function (party) { return controlled.includes(party); }) &&
                (Q.burdens_start_countdown > 0 || Q.burdens_start_trigger || Q.burdens_goal > 0 && Q.burdens_time > 0))
                Q.burdens_done += 1;
            // A narrow departmental agreement: fiscal effects settle over twelve
            // ticks; this strike owns its single electoral delivery award.
        }

        var cabinet = Array.from(new Set(Q.cat_coalition || []));
        function ballot(party) {
            if (party == "ciu") party = Q.parlament_current_ciu;
            if (party == "fl" || party == "federal_left") party = Q.parlament_current_icv;
            for (var list of ["jxsi", "jxcat"])
                if (Q[party + "_in_" + list] && (Q.parties || []).includes(list) &&
                    (Q.parlament_constituencies || []).some(function (province) {
                        return (Q.parlament_demographics || []).some(function (demo) { return Q[list + "_parlament_" + province + "_" + demo + "_support"] > 0; });
                    })) return list;
            return party;
        }
        var player = ballot(Q.player_party);
        cabinet = Array.from(new Set(cabinet.map(ballot)));
        var minister = ballot(Q.strike_university_partner);
        var left = Array.from(new Set(["erc", "cup", Q.parlament_current_icv].map(ballot)))
            .filter(function (party) { return (Q.parties || []).includes(party); });
        var oppositionLeft = left.filter(function (party) { return !cabinet.includes(party) && party != player; });

        // Explicit province/demographic cells: no uniform national polling bonus.
        var profile = [
            ["barcelona","young",0.65],
            ["barcelona","middle",0.20],
            ["barcelona","unemployed",0.15],
            ["girona","young",0.45],
            ["girona","middle",0.12],
            ["girona","unemployed",0.10],
            ["lleida","young",0.40],
            ["lleida","middle",0.12],
            ["lleida","unemployed",0.10],
            ["tarragona","young",0.50],
            ["tarragona","middle",0.18],
            ["tarragona","unemployed",0.12]
        ];
        var credit = [];
        if (delivery) {
            var partners = cabinet.filter(function (party) { return party != player; });
            credit.push([player, response == "pressure" ? 0.4 : partners.length ? 0.8 : 1]);
            if (response == "pressure") credit.push([minister,0.6]);
            else for (var party of partners) credit.push([party,0.2 / partners.length]);
        }
        // All routes use the shared conserving helper (including successor/list
        // resolution, donor caps and independence saturation).
        function transfer(from, to, amount, cell) {
            from = ballot(from); to = ballot(to);
            if (!from || !to || from == to || !(Q.parties || []).concat(["abstain"]).includes(from) ||
                !(Q.parties || []).concat(["abstain"]).includes(to)) return;
            G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, {contest:"parlament", from:from, to:to, amount:amount,
                maxDonorFraction:0.5, constituencies:[cell[0]], demographics:[cell[1]]});
        }
        for (var cell of profile) {
            var amount = cell[2];
            if (delivery) {
                for (var recipient of credit) {
                    var donors = recipient[0] == ballot("cup") ? [["fl",0.45],["erc",0.30],["abstain",0.25]] :
                        recipient[0] == ballot("erc") ? [["psc",0.45],["fl",0.30],["abstain",0.25]] :
                        [["psc",0.35],["fl",0.25],["abstain",0.40]];
                    for (var donor of donors) transfer(donor[0],recipient[0],amount * recipient[1] * donor[1],cell);
                }
            } else {
                // A silent opposition player does not collect the government's
                // losses. Other opposition parties still gain from mobilization.
                var challengers = oppositionLeft.slice();
                if (response == "protest" && !challengers.includes(player)) challengers.push(player);
                for (var incumbent of cabinet) {
                    var responsibility = incumbent == minister ? 1 : 0.4;
                    if (incumbent == player && incumbent != minister) responsibility = 0.6;
                    var destinations = challengers.filter(function (party) { return party != incumbent; });
                    for (var destination of destinations)
                        transfer(incumbent,destination,amount * responsibility * 0.6 / destinations.length,cell);
                    transfer(incumbent,"abstain",amount * responsibility * 0.2,cell);
                }
                for (var destination of challengers) {
                    transfer("psc",destination,amount * 0.10 / challengers.length,cell);
                    transfer("abstain",destination,amount * 0.10 / challengers.length,cell);
                }
                if ((Q.cat_coalition_support || []).some(function (party) { return controlled.includes(party); }) && !cabinet.includes(player)) {
                    for (var destination of oppositionLeft)
                        transfer(player,destination,amount * 0.25 / oppositionLeft.length,cell);
                }
            }
        }

        // Relations concern the actual parties, rather than pooled vote carriers.
        for (var party of ["erc", "cup", Q.parlament_current_icv]) {
            if (!controlled.includes(ballot(party)) && Number.isFinite(Q[party + "_relations"]))
                Q[party + "_relations"] += response == "quiet" ? -2 : 2;
        }
        if (response == "pressure" || response == "protest" || response == "quiet" && !controlled.includes(Q.strike_university_partner) &&
            (Q.cat_coalition || []).concat(Q.cat_coalition_support || []).some(function (party) { return controlled.includes(party); }))
            Q[Q.strike_university_partner + "_relations"] = (Q.strike_university_relations || 0) + (response == "quiet" ? 2 : response == "pressure" ? -3 : -4);
    }
!}
call: generalitat_setpolicy

[? if strike_university_settled: [? if response == "pressure" : Thanks to our efforts, ?][? if education_minister_gender = "m": Conseller ?][? if education_minister_gender = "f": Consellera ?]of Education [+ education_minister +] has reached an agreement with union representatives, and tuition fees will be lowered. Further strikes have been called off and the situation seems to have calmed down, at least for now.  ?]
[? if not strike_university_settled: With angry students on the street and a Ministry deeply against any concession that would put further strain on Generalitat finances, it looks like the labour dispute is here to stay. ?]

- @post_event: Continue
